investigation.theirEncoding:
WG item 14234 has exactly ONE operation:
  {"id":"c96e36a4-2e79-4460-93e9-9b3b107d6e1c","type":"adjValue","data":{"variable":"WEAKNESSES","value":"fire, 5"}}
i.e. adjValue WEAKNESSES = "fire, 5". WG encodes nothing else mechanical (no Reflex-DC bonus, no flat-check change, no activations).

investigation.fixSpec:
Add ONE row to scripts/data/effect-backfill.json (top-level array):
{"category":"items","id":"arboreals-revenge","field":"passiveEffects","value":{"weaknesses":[{"type":"fire","value":5}]}}
Exact precedent already in the file: {"category":"items","id":"demons-knot","field":"passiveEffects","value":{"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold-iron","value":10},{"type":"holy","value":10}],"immunities":["confused","controlled"]}} — which is present in public/core.json items['demons-knot'].passiveEffects today, proving the overlay applier handles category=items + field=passiveEffects. Use passiveEffects.weaknesses, NOT a top-level `weaknesses` (types.ts:2042 warns top-level on an item is the un-canonical home). Reader picking it up: derive.ts:2403-2422 -> deriveDefenses -> DefensesPills.tsx:59 / VitalsRail.tsx:781. Do not touch situationalBonuses.ts:1285 (the +4 Reflex DC is a print clause WG omits and must stay). Out of scope but noted: items.arboreals-revenge.heldSpells lists "cleanse-affliction", which print only names as a spell that FAILS to remove the item — likely a bad extraction, separate ticket.

Append two rows to scripts/data/effect-backfill.json (shape {category,id,field,value}; applied last by scripts/import-core-v2.mjs:715-721; dedupe key is category|id|field):
1) {"category":"feats","id":"grave-mummification","field":"senses","value":[{"name":"darkvision"}]}
2) {"category":"feats","id":"grave-mummification","field":"resistances","value":[{"type":"poison","value":"max(1,floor(@actor.level/2))"},{"type":"damage from your bound terrain (dangerous temperatures, weather, hazardous terrain and environmental hazards)","value":"floor(@actor.level/2)"}]}
Both land on public/core.json feats.grave-mummification and are picked up by derive.ts:2365-2368 -> 2501/2505. Free-text resistance types are an established shape here: feats.crystal-keeper-dedication uses "damage from hazards associated with crystals" and feats.one-among-the-masses uses "damage from swarms, troops, and creatures sharing your space" (both resolve through the same loop; a free-text type simply prints as its own IWR line). Leave situationalBonuses.ts:2996 alone — the two save stars already match WG's four addBonusToValue ops. Do NOT edit public/core.json directly.

